      "writtenOn": "2026-11-06T04:25:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Job creation is a side effect of the PATCH (`patch_bios` sends `SettingsApplyTime: OnReset`, which schedules the BIOS config job on iDRAC9 per the comment at `external/badfish.py:987`). If the staged value outlived its job, for example a failed or deleted job, this shortcut returns True without a job to apply it. The reboot then cannot apply the mode, `_wait_for_bootmode` burns the full 600s, and the next attempt takes the same path. Suggest PATCHing anyway or checking for a scheduled job before returning here.",
      "revId": "fca26fed4336e1982580ad7002c85dd84097c8c9",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
