      "writtenOn": "2026-11-06T04:25:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`get_request` does not check the response status, so a 401/500 body that is valid JSON is parsed and the missing `Attributes` key returns None, the same value as \u0027no pending change\u0027. The dispatcher also catches exceptions and returns None. `_ensure_bootmode` treats None as no conflict, so a failed Settings read silently disables the guard this change adds. Suggest distinguishing \u0027could not read\u0027 from \u0027no pending value\u0027, so the release layer can abort instead of assuming the pending area is clean.",
      "revId": "fca26fed4336e1982580ad7002c85dd84097c8c9",
